TESTDATA["pet4-t1"] = {"title":"Cambridge PET 4 · Test 1","format":"2010","reading":[{"part":1,"items":[{"n":1,"text":"UNIVERSITY LIBRARY\nPlease wait here while we check your books","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Do not go away until we have checked your books.","Check you have all your books before you leave the library.","Do not leave books here for checking without telling us."],"answer":"A"},{"n":2,"text":"To: Sally   From: Kim\nFeeling any better? When you're back at college, remember to register for the fun course. Email me if you want any information about it.","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"Why has Kim emailed Sally?","options":["to give her some details","to let her know that he'll see her","to remind her to do something"],"answer":"C"},{"n":3,"text":"HOSPITAL WAITING ROOM\nPLEASE PUT ALL CHILDREN'S TOYS BACK IN THIS ROOM BEFORE YOU LEAVE","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["We leave some toys at the back of this room for children.","Please don't leave any toys outside this room when you go.","Remember to take your children's toys with you when you leave."],"answer":"B"},{"n":4,"text":"Ed,\nDennis rang! DON'T take the main road to Madleigh – there's been an accident and you won't get to the match on time. Go through Drayton instead.\nLynn","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["To arrive punctually, Ed should use a different route.","Dennis suggests that it's quicker to go on the main road.","If there's enough time, Lynn would like to see the match."],"answer":"A"},{"n":5,"text":"Not as big a city as we expected, but that's okay. Limited nightlife, though there's plenty to see every day and travelling around is painless!\nMartyna","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"According to Martyna, the city's disadvantage is","options":["its actual size.","its transport system.","its evening entertainment."],"answer":"C"}]},{"part":2,"people":[{"n":6,"name":"Anna","text":"Anna is 18 and she wants to do computer studies so that she can work in an office. She would like to study in London but is worried about finding accommodation.","answer":"D"},{"n":7,"name":"Peter","text":"Peter is 19 and wants to be a sports teacher. He is very good at sport, especially running. He wants to go to a college outside London.","answer":"B"},{"n":8,"name":"Maria","text":"Maria used to teach in a secondary school but now wants to teach at primary level. She wants to do a part-time course in London.","answer":"G"},{"n":9,"name":"Stephen","text":"Stephen works in the computer industry and wants to go back to college for a year to do a diploma in advanced computer studies. He lives in London and wants to study there.","answer":"H"},{"n":10,"name":"Ali","text":"Ali wants to do computer studies in London. He would like to do a full-time course which includes some time working in industry. In his spare time he plays football.","answer":"E"}],"texts":[{"letter":"A","title":"Hillman College","text":"Hillman College is a London college with up-to-date facilities. We offer both primary and secondary full-time teacher training courses. This year there will be special two-year courses available on maths and computers in the primary classroom. All students are expected to spend two terms working in local schools."},{"letter":"B","title":"Kirby College","text":"Kirby College has over fifty years' experience of teacher training. We offer both full-time and part-time courses for all levels of teaching. Large college in lovely countryside, with excellent sports facilities, especially for football and athletics. There is a new course this year called 'Computers in the Classroom'."},{"letter":"C","title":"Kemp College","text":"Kemp College offers a wide range of both full-time and part-time diploma courses in arts and science subjects, lasting from one to three years. The college is about two hours away from London by train. It has a new library and good student accommodation. Grants are available for students wanting to return to studying."},{"letter":"D","title":"MacKintosh College","text":"MacKintosh College offers a range of courses from modern languages to computer studies, in a quiet and pleasant part of London. All students are offered accommodation in college flats and we have excellent sports facilities. Full-time and part-time courses of either three or four years are available."},{"letter":"E","title":"Pemberley College","text":"Pemberley College in central London offers full-time courses in science and computer studies. Our four-year courses allow you to spend a term every year getting work experience in different firms. There are good social and sports facilities. No college accommodation is available at present."},{"letter":"F","title":"Treeholme College","text":"If you want to be a teacher, join one of our courses. Places are available on our full-time courses in science and maths this October. Ours is a small teacher training department in a large London college, so we can offer good facilities such as a new computer centre."},{"letter":"G","title":"Dene College","text":"Dene College was built in 1990 in an attractive part of north London. Spaces are still available on our popular part-time course in primary teaching for teachers who want to retrain. Beginning in October we will also have new four-year courses in law, economics, mathematics and sports science."},{"letter":"H","title":"Westgate College","text":"Westgate College in south London has a range of courses, from maths and physics to computer studies and sports science. We offer both lower and advanced diplomas. All our courses are from one to three years in length and are particularly suitable for people with some work experience."}]},{"part":3,"title":"European travel","text":"TAKE THIS GREAT OPPORTUNITY TO DISCOVER SOME WONDERFUL EUROPEAN CITIES\n\nHere is a wonderful flight offer from the Daily News, giving our readers the chance to get a return ticket to Europe for next to nothing.\n\nEuropean destinations\nOur basic offer price of £10 allows you to take an Express Airlines flight to Brussels in Belgium from Heathrow Airport in London. At Brussels Airport there are connections to Nice, Milan, Madrid or Copenhagen for only an extra £25 return.\nThis offer is available from November to February, apart from the period December 18–January 6. There are up to five flights during the day between Heathrow and Brussels. If you plan to travel further than Brussels, you will need to get to the airport early in the morning. However, a charge of £10 is added to the ticket price for travel between Friday and Sunday.\n\nSo much to see and do\nWhy not treat yourself and your partner or friend to a few days in Belgium? Discover wonderful Brussels, which is much more than the centre of the European Union. The Belgian capital is a mix of old and new, with a historic central square, a number of galleries and museums to explore, and more restaurants per person than any other city in Europe. The Daily News is also organising tours of the beautiful Belgian towns of Bruges and Antwerp. There is also the opportunity for our readers to stay at the Crown Inn Hotel in Brussels and enjoy luxury accommodation and friendly service for an amazing price starting from £15 per person per night. The Crown Inn Hotel is in a perfect position for you to see the sights and look round the city shops. Or you can simply relax in this friendly hotel, which offers leisure facilities and family rooms, making it a great place for people with children.\n\nHow to get your tickets\nWe will only consider bookings made on the special application form printed in our newspaper, and sent to us with a cheque for the fare. One week before departure, please contact our office by phone to check your booking.\nWe recommend that you get travel insurance for your trip. Please note that the prices do not include airport tax. Once bookings are made, no changes are allowed, and your money cannot be refunded if you cancel. Any flight may be changed or cancelled by the airline company without notice.","items":[{"n":11,"q":"The Daily News is offering free flights to a number of European cities.","answer":"B"},{"n":12,"q":"These tickets allow passengers to fly directly from Heathrow to Nice.","answer":"B"},{"n":13,"q":"To go to Copenhagen you must leave early in the morning.","answer":"A"},{"n":14,"q":"Travelling on Saturdays costs extra.","answer":"A"},{"n":15,"q":"The Crown Inn Hotel is convenient for shopping.","answer":"A"},{"n":16,"q":"You must write to the newspaper for a special application form.","answer":"B"},{"n":17,"q":"You should ring the newspaper about your reservation seven days before you are due to leave.","answer":"A"},{"n":18,"q":"Passengers must buy insurance for the trip.","answer":"B"},{"n":19,"q":"You must pay extra for airport tax.","answer":"A"},{"n":20,"q":"The airline company has the right to change a flight without telling passengers in advance.","answer":"A"}]},{"part":4,"title":"","text":"John Fisher, a builder, and his wife Elizabeth wanted more living space, so they left their small flat for an old 40-metre-high castle tower. They have spent five years turning it into a beautiful home with six floors, winning three architectural prizes.\n\n'I love the space, and being private,' Elizabeth says. 'You feel separated from the world. If I'm in the kitchen, which is 25 metres above the ground floor, and the doorbell rings, I don't have to answer it because visitors can't see I'm in!'\n\n'There are 142 steps to the top, so if I go up and down five or six times a day, it's very good exercise! But having to carry heavy things to the top is terrible, so I never buy more than two bags of shopping from the supermarket at a time. Apart from that, it's a brilliant place to live.'\n\n'When we first saw the place, I asked my father's advice about buying it, because we couldn't decide. After paying for it, we were a bit worried because it looked awful. But we really loved it, and knew how we wanted it to look.'\n\n'Living here can be difficult – yesterday I climbed a four-metre ladder to clean the windows. But when you stand on the roof you can see all the way out to sea on a clear day, and that's a wonderful experience. I'm really glad we moved.'","items":[{"n":21,"q":"What is the writer trying to do in the text?","options":["describe how to turn an old tower into a house","recommend a particular builder","describe what it is like to live in a tower","explain how to win prizes for building work"],"answer":"C"},{"n":22,"q":"From this text, a reader can find out","options":["why visitors are not welcome at John and Elizabeth's house.","why Elizabeth exercises every day.","why Elizabeth asked her father to buy the tower.","why John and Elizabeth left their flat."],"answer":"D"},{"n":23,"q":"Which of the following best describes Elizabeth's feelings about the tower?","options":["She wanted it as soon as she saw it.","She likes most things about it.","She has been worried since they paid for it.","She finds it unsuitable to live in."],"answer":"B"},{"n":24,"q":"What problem does Elizabeth have with living in such a tall building?","options":["Her visitors find it difficult to see if she is at home.","She feels separated from other people.","She cannot bring home lots of shopping at once.","It is impossible to clean any of the windows."],"answer":"C"},{"n":25,"q":"How will John and Elizabeth advertise the tower if they sell it?","options":["FOR SALE — Tall building, formerly a castle. High windows give a good view. Needs some improvement.","FOR SALE — A house with a difference – a castle tower, turned into a lovely home. Wonderful view.","FOR SALE — Prize-winning home, five years old. Six rooms, all with sea views.","FOR SALE — Castle tower, turned into six small flats, close to supermarket."],"answer":"B"}]},{"part":5,"title":"CAMPING","text":"Although (0) ……… (some) groups of people have always lived outdoors in tents, camping as we know it today only began to be [26] about 50 years ago. The increase in the use of cars and improvements in camping [27] have allowed more people to travel longer [28] into the countryside and to stay there in greater comfort.\nMany campers like to be [29] themselves in quiet areas, so they [30] their tent and food and walk or cycle into the forests or the mountains. Others, preferring to be near people, drive to a public or privately-owned campsite [31] has up-to-date facilities, [32] as hot showers and swimming pools.\nWhether campers are [33] in the mountains or on a busy site, they should remember to [34] the area clean and tidy. In the forests, they must put out any fires and keep food hidden to avoid attracting [35] animals.","gaps":{"26":{"options":["famous","popular","favourite","current"],"answer":"B"},"27":{"options":["tools","baggage","equipment","property"],"answer":"C"},"28":{"options":["ways","directions","voyages","distances"],"answer":"D"},"29":{"options":["on","by","at","of"],"answer":"B"},"30":{"options":["take","make","pick","do"],"answer":"A"},"31":{"options":["where","who","which","when"],"answer":"C"},"32":{"options":["such","like","as","just"],"answer":"B"},"33":{"options":["lonely","single","separate","alone"],"answer":"D"},"34":{"options":["remain","stay","leave","let"],"answer":"C"},"35":{"options":["wild","natural","loose","free"],"answer":"A"}}}],"writing":[{"part":1,"title":"Here are some sentences about a student who is living in a flat.","items":[{"n":1,"first":"My friend told me that I could stay in his flat.","before":"My friend said: 'You","after":"my flat.'","answers":["can stay in","can stay at"]},{"n":2,"first":"I started living here two months ago.","before":"I have lived here","after":"two months ago.","answers":["since"]},{"n":3,"first":"This is the first time I've lived in a city.","before":"I've","after":"in a city before.","answers":["never lived"]},{"n":4,"first":"The flat has two bedrooms.","before":"There","after":"in the flat.","answers":["are two bedrooms","are 2 bedrooms"]},{"n":5,"first":"My bedroom is too small for all my books.","before":"My bedroom is not","after":"for all my books.","answers":["large enough","big enough"]}]},{"part":2,"items":[{"n":6,"kind":"message","task":"You have just joined a club in your area and you think your English friend Max would enjoy going there with you too.\n\nWrite an email to Max. In your email, you should\n• explain which club you have joined\n• suggest Max should visit the club\n• say what you could do there together.\n\nWrite 35–45 words on your answer sheet.","points":["dire a quale club si è iscritto/a","proporre a Max di iscriversi","dire che cosa possono fare insieme lì"]}]},{"part":3,"items":[{"n":7,"kind":"letter","task":"This is part of a letter you receive from a friend in the U.S.A.\n\n'I guess there are many traditional festivals in your country. What's the most important one? Why do people celebrate this festival? Write and tell me all about it!'\n\nNow write a letter, answering your friend's questions.\nWrite your letter in about 100 words on your answer sheet."},{"n":8,"kind":"story","task":"Your English teacher has asked you to write a story.\nYour story must begin with this sentence:\n\nNobody knew what Adam had in his suitcase.\n\nWrite your story in about 100 words on your answer sheet."}]}],"listening":[{"part":1,"audio":"audio/pet4-t1-l1.mp3","items":[{"n":1,"q":"Which activity will the family do this year?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":2,"q":"Which is the woman's house?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"A"},{"n":3,"q":"Why will drivers have problems this morning?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":4,"q":"What time will Robin leave the house?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":5,"q":"What did Simon do this morning?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":6,"q":"What hasn't the girl packed yet?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":7,"q":"What has the woman just bought?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"A"}],"example":"img/pet4-t1-l1-ex.jpg"},{"part":2,"intro":"You will hear an interview with Angela Morgan, who has recently flown around the world in a helicopter.","audio":"audio/pet4-t1-l2.mp3","items":[{"n":8,"q":"The main reason for Angela's trip was to","options":["make money for her business.","make money for other people.","have an exciting adventure."],"answer":"B"},{"n":9,"q":"What does Angela say about her life now?","options":["She feels much older.","She likes to be active and busy.","She is lonely without her children."],"answer":"B"},{"n":10,"q":"When Angela had flying lessons","options":["her course lasted five months.","her husband took lessons as well.","she got to know her teacher well."],"answer":"C"},{"n":11,"q":"During the trip, Angela and her teacher","options":["did very little sightseeing.","carried all the water they needed.","had engine problems several times."],"answer":"A"},{"n":12,"q":"What did Angela enjoy most about the trip?","options":["flying at night","walking in the desert","watching the changes in the scenery"],"answer":"C"},{"n":13,"q":"What did Angela miss most while she was away?","options":["modern bathrooms","regular exercise","interesting entertainment"],"answer":"B"}]},{"part":3,"intro":"You will hear a radio announcer talking about activities at a museum called Science World.","audio":"audio/pet4-t1-l3.mp3","notes":"Science World\nNext week's Special Events\n\nEVENTS: TIME OF DAY:\nElectricity workshop — [14]\nExperiments with water — Wednesday morning\nTalk about space travel by well-known scientist from [15] — Saturday evening\n\nScience World entrance fees: £3.00 Adults / £2.00 Children\nTickets for Special Events cost extra: £ [16] Adults\nReduced prices for children\nGet tickets direct from Science World on 284311, or from the [17].\nNewton Café is next to the [18] (snacks available all day).\nPhone Science World for free ticket to exhibition about [19].","answers":{"14":["Monday afternoon","Monday p.m.","Monday pm"],"15":["America","U.S.A.","USA","United States of America","United States","the United States of America","the United States"],"16":["£1.75","1.75"],"17":["tourist offices","tourist office"],"18":["beach"],"19":["computers","computer"]}},{"part":4,"intro":"You will hear a conversation between a boy, Tom, and his sister, Clare, about school.","audio":"audio/pet4-t1-l4.mp3","items":[{"n":20,"q":"Clare thinks their father will be pleased by Tom's news.","answer":"B"},{"n":21,"q":"Tom believes he can manage both swimming and school work.","answer":"A"},{"n":22,"q":"Tom's teacher thinks Tom is clever.","answer":"A"},{"n":23,"q":"Tom dislikes doing maths.","answer":"B"},{"n":24,"q":"Clare thinks it is a bad idea to take a friend's advice.","answer":"A"},{"n":25,"q":"Tom finally realises he will need his father's agreement to his plans.","answer":"A"}]}]};
